---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
    title="Privacy policy — Lustre Clinic"
    description="What Lustre Clinic handles, where it is stored, and what is done with Google account data."
>
    <div class="page">

        <header class="masthead">
            <span class="eyebrow">Lustre Clinic</span>
            <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
            <p class="lede">
                Lustre is clinic management software for dental practices. This page says what it handles,
                where that is kept, and what is done with access to a Google account. It also covers this
                website.
            </p>
            <p class="meta">Last updated 1 October 2026.</p>
        </header>

        <h2>Who this is</h2>
        <p>
            Lustre is built and maintained by Youssef Hany Galal. It is offered to dental practices and
            set up at each one in person. There is no public sign-up and no shared online service: every
            clinic runs its own copy, on a computer that clinic owns, used by its own dentist and
            secretary. One clinic's copy has no connection to another's.
        </p>

        <h2>Clinic records</h2>
        <p>
            Each clinic's records — patients, appointments, visits, procedures and payments — are stored
            in a database on a computer inside that clinic. That computer belongs to the clinic.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>These records are <b>not</b> sent to the developer, and are not hosted on any cloud service.</li>
            <li>Reaching the software requires being on that clinic's private network. There is no public address.</li>
            <li>Each clinic is the controller of its own patient data and is responsible for it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            The one exception is the off-site backup described next, and it is encrypted.
        </p>

        <h2>Google account data</h2>

        <h3>What is requested</h3>
        <p>
            Exactly one permission: <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
            This permission is limited by Google to files the application itself created. Lustre
            <b>cannot</b> list, read, alter or delete anything else in the account's Google Drive, and
            does not ask for any permission that would let it.
        </p>

        <h3>What it is used for</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Creating one folder, <b>Lustre Clinic Backups</b>, in the signed-in account's Drive.</li>
            <li>Uploading the nightly backup of the clinic database into that folder.</li>
            <li>Listing the backups that folder holds, so old ones can be removed on a schedule.</li>
            <li>Deleting backups that have aged out — roughly 14 daily, 8 weekly and 12 monthly are kept.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Nothing else. Google account data is not used for analytics, advertising, profiling, training
            any model, or any purpose unrelated to storing and pruning these backups.
        </p>

        <h3>The backup contents</h3>
        <p>
            A backup is a copy of the clinic's database, so it contains patient records. It is
            <b>encrypted on the clinic computer before it is uploaded</b>. The encryption key is not kept
            on that computer, is not uploaded with the backup, and is not known to Google or to the
            developer. What is stored in Drive is ciphertext.
        </p>

        <h3>Credentials</h3>
        <p>
            When a clinic's dentist signs in, Google issues a refresh token. That token is stored on the
            clinic's own server, in a file readable only by the account the server runs as. It is not
            transmitted to the developer and is not stored on any phone. Short-lived access tokens are
            held in memory only and never written to disk.
        </p>

        <h3>Sharing</h3>
        <p>
            Google account data and backup contents are not sold, rented, or shared with anyone. There
            are no third-party analytics, advertising or tracking services in the application.
        </p>

        <div class="panel">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0">Limited Use</h3>
            <p style="margin-bottom: 0">
                Lustre's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
                <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User
                    Data Policy</a>,
                including the Limited Use requirements.
            </p>
        </div>

        <h2>Withdrawing access</h2>
        <p>
            The signed-in account can revoke Lustre's access at any time at
            <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
            Backups already in Drive are unaffected and remain the account holder's to keep or delete.
            Once revoked, the clinic's off-site copies stop; the software reports this so it is noticed
            rather than discovered later.
        </p>

        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>
            Backups in Drive are pruned automatically on the schedule above. Deleting the
            <b>Lustre Clinic Backups</b> folder removes them all. Records held on the clinic's own server
            are retained by the practice according to its own obligations.
        </p>

        <h2>Crash reports</h2>
        <p>
            Errors from the phone application are collected to diagnose faults. They are sent to software
            running on the clinic's own server, not to any third-party service, and are limited to error
            codes, screen names and application version. Patient names, phone numbers, notes and amounts
            are excluded.
        </p>

        <h2>This website</h2>
        <p>
            lustresystems.com sets no cookies and runs no analytics, advertising or tracking. It remembers
            a light or dark choice in your own browser, and nothing else. Its fonts come from Google Fonts
            and its icons from unpkg, which, like any web server, see your IP address when they send them.
        </p>

        <h2>If you contact us</h2>
        <p>
            If you write to us by email or WhatsApp, we use what you send only to reply and to talk with
            you about setting Lustre up at your clinic. It is not shared, sold, or added to any mailing
            list.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
            If what the software does with Google account data changes, this page changes with it, and
            the date at the top is updated.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
            <a href="mailto:privacy@lustresystems.com">privacy@lustresystems.com</a>
        </p>

        <footer>
            <p>
                <a href="/">Lustre</a> ·
                <a href="https://github.com/lustre-systems/lustre-clinic">Source</a>
            </p>
        </footer>

    </div>
</Layout>
